  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nConfidence remains high in accumulating snowfall this Friday \nand Saturday. A low pressure center is expected to cross into \nthe Ohio Valley tonight bringing some showers to the region \nthrough the day on Thursday. Probabilities continue to show a \ntrend of 20% to 30% in the low lands and 50% to 70% in the\nhigher terrain of exceeding 0.50\". The frontal passage is \nexpected to occur by 05Z Friday with much of the precip changing\nto snow showers with Lake Enhanced snowfall expected. \n\nAt this time, the main impact will be over the the WV Ridges.\n80% to 90% probability of exceeding advisory criteria is\nexpected in the WV mountains. \n\nExpect a slower system passing through the the area a bit more \nnorth, or just above the Mason Dixon Line, would produce a \nscenario closer to the outcome described above. This would bring\nadvisory snow to the WV mountains and potentially the northern \ncounties but the northern counties reaching advisory criteria is\na 10% to 20% probability.",
